# Daedalus owner allowed signers -- the trust root for sealed promotion approval.
#
# This file, at its committed revision, is what decides whose signature counts
# as the repository owner's. It is read by
# daedalus/kernel/signed_approval.py through `git show HEAD:<this path>`, never
# from the working tree, so editing the checked-out copy grants nothing.
#
# Format is ssh-keygen(1) ALLOWED SIGNERS. One principal per line:
#
#   owner@daedalus ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA... comment
#
# The principal on the left must match the signing identity (user.email) the
# owner tags with.
#
# It is deliberately empty of principals. Promotion approval is refused --
# SignedApprovalRootError -- until the owner adds their own public key in a
# reviewed commit. An empty root is the correct default: it fails closed, and
# it cannot be filled in by anything that merely runs as the owner.
#
# Adding a key here is a trust-root change. It belongs in its own commit, with
# the key fingerprint stated in the message, and it should be reviewed as
# carefully as a change to the promotion boundary itself.
#
# See docs/OWNER_SEALED_APPROVAL_HOWTO.md for minting a key and signing.
